# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — never commit. Rulebook Appendix A + Appendix E rules 39-40.
# A secret pushed even once is permanently compromised: removing it from the
# current tree is NOT enough, it stays in git history and the credentials must
# be rotated in the Google Cloud console. This applies even to a private repo
# shared only with the lecturer.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
credentials.json
token.json
token*.json
client_secret*.json
.env
*.env
config/**/secrets*
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling caches and coverage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# NOTE: match artefacts are deliberately NOT ignored. Per-match config files
# must be committed (Appendix F, mandatory rule 4), and match logs are the
# evidence the Replay App verifies.

# Gatekeeper runtime state: the daily quota ledger and the DoS lock. Machine-
# local counters, not code — and untracked-but-not-ignored files used to be
# counted as a dirty tree, which is the one thing they must never be.
.quota_*.json
.dos_lock_*
